.TH pvc-spectrummapper 1  "pvc-spectrummapper " 
.SH NAME
pvc\-spectrummapper \- Track formant peaks into continuous tracks
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpvc\-spectrummapper\fR <\fB\-\-segments\-file\fR> [\fB\-\-scatter\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-ascii\-segments\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-fft\fR] [\fB\-\-window\-size\fR] [\fB\-\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-frames\-per\-sec\fR] [\fB\-\-begin\fR] [\fB\-\-end\fR] [\fB\-\-channel\fR] [\fB\-\-eq\-bypass\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-freq\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-freq\fR] [\fB\-\-low\-freq\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-high\-freq\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-formant\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-formant\-threshold\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-decibels\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-decibels\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-segment\-length\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-segment\-length\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-segment\-duration\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-segment\-duration\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-freq\-change\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-db\-rise\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-db\-fall\fR] [\fB\-\-linkage\-time\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-freq\-linkage\fR] [\fB\-\-onset\-release\-mode\fR] [\fB\-\-onset\-duration\fR] [\fB\-\-release\-duration\fR] [\fB\-\-time\-shift\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIINPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Formant\-*tracking* analysis tool: extracts formant peaks frame by frame from raw audio, greedily assembles them into time\-continuous segments (tracks), links separate segments into longer chains, and writes the result to ASCII/binary formant\-track files. Writes no audio output at all.
.PP
Ports `spectrummapper` (`legacy/pvc_src/spectrummapper.c`); see `pvc\-core::tools::spectrummapper`\*(Aqs doc comment for what\*(Aqs in and out of scope, including a real amplitude\-rescale bug that double\-applies a frame\*(Aqs own peak amplitude whenever that peak is `>= 1.0`, and a real `dB_to_amp`\-for\-`amp_to_dB` copy\-paste bug in the "impose" onset envelope.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-segments\-file\fR \fI<SEGMENTS_FILE>\fR
`\-S`: path to write the binary formant\-track file. Required \- the real C would otherwise `fwrite` through a null `FILE*` from a failed `fopen("", ...)`
.TP
\fB\-\-scatter\-file\fR \fI<SCATTER_FILE>\fR
`\-f`: path to write an ASCII scatter plot of every raw per\-frame formant point (time, frequency). Omit to skip writing it
.TP
\fB\-\-ascii\-segments\-file\fR \fI<ASCII_SEGMENTS_FILE>\fR
`\-a`: path to write an ASCII listing of the final linked segments. Omit to skip writing it
.TP
\fB\-\-fft\fR \fI<FFT>\fR [default: 1024]
`\-N`: FFT size
.TP
\fB\-\-window\-size\fR \fI<WINDOW_SIZE>\fR [default: 2048]
`\-M`: analysis window length. `0` means auto (`2 * fft`)
.TP
\fB\-\-window\fR \fI<WINDOW>\fR [default: hamming]

.TP
\fB\-\-frames\-per\-sec\fR \fI<FRAMES_PER_SEC>\fR [default: 200]
`\-D`: analysis frames per second (sets the hop size). Values under `32` reset to `200`
.TP
\fB\-\-begin\fR \fI<BEGIN>\fR [default: 0]
`\-b`: begin time in seconds \- real sample\-accurate trimming
.TP
\fB\-\-end\fR \fI<END>\fR [default: 0]
`\-e`: end time in seconds (`0` = end of file)
.TP
\fB\-\-channel\fR \fI<CHANNEL>\fR [default: 0]
`\-C`: which input channel to analyze (`0` = all channels, each processed independently; `1..` = only that one, 1\-based)
.TP
\fB\-\-eq\-bypass\fR
`\-B`: bypass the shelf EQ entirely (`0` = apply it, the default; `1` = bypass)
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-gain\fR \fI<SHELF_LOW_GAIN>\fR [default: 0]
`\-H`: low shelf EQ gain in dB
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-gain\fR \fI<SHELF_HIGH_GAIN>\fR [default: 0]
`\-X`: high shelf EQ gain in dB
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-freq\fR \fI<SHELF_LOW_FREQ>\fR [default: 200]
`\-m`: low shelf EQ frequency in Hz
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-freq\fR \fI<SHELF_HIGH_FREQ>\fR [default: 2000]
`\-R`: high shelf EQ frequency in Hz
.TP
\fB\-\-low\-freq\-limit\fR \fI<LOW_FREQ_LIMIT>\fR [default: 0]
`\-L`: low frequency limit in Hz for formant selection \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-high\-freq\-limit\fR \fI<HIGH_FREQ_LIMIT>\fR [default: 0]
`\-j`: high frequency limit in Hz for formant selection (`<= 0` means Nyquist) \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-formant\-db\fR \fI<MINIMUM_FORMANT_DB>\fR [default: \-96]
`\-A`: minimum formant peak amplitude in dB
.TP
\fB\-\-formant\-threshold\fR \fI<FORMANT_SELECTION_THRESHOLD>\fR [default: 0.5]
`\-g`: formant selection/rejection threshold, `0`\-`1`. Higher values select fewer, stronger formants
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-decibels\fR \fI<MINIMUM_DECIBELS>\fR [default: \-200]
`\-c`: minimum decibel level for a formant to remain eligible for segment construction
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-decibels\fR \fI<MAXIMUM_DECIBELS>\fR [default: 0]
`\-E`: maximum decibel level for a formant to remain eligible
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-segment\-length\fR \fI<MINIMUM_SEGMENT_LENGTH>\fR [default: 1]
`\-o`: minimum final segment length in frames
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-segment\-length\fR \fI<MAXIMUM_SEGMENT_LENGTH>\fR [default: 0]
`\-O`: maximum final segment length in frames (`<= 0` = unlimited)
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-segment\-duration\fR \fI<MINIMUM_SEGMENT_DURATION>\fR [default: 0]
`\-q`: minimum final segment duration in seconds
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-segment\-duration\fR \fI<MAXIMUM_SEGMENT_DURATION>\fR [default: 0]
`\-Q`: maximum final segment duration in seconds (`<= 0` means twice the analysis duration)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-freq\-change\fR \fI<MAX_FREQUENCY_CHANGE_PER_MS>\fR [default: 12]
`\-p`: maximum frequency change per millisecond allowed while growing a segment
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-db\-rise\fR \fI<MAX_DECIBEL_RISE_PER_MS>\fR [default: 90]
`\-V`: maximum decibel rise per millisecond allowed while growing a segment
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-db\-fall\fR \fI<MAX_DECIBEL_FALL_PER_MS>\fR [default: 90]
`\-v`: maximum decibel fall per millisecond allowed while growing a segment
.TP
\fB\-\-linkage\-time\fR \fI<LINKAGE_TIME>\fR [default: 0.02]
`\-r`: maximum time gap in seconds allowed when linking two segments together
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-freq\-linkage\fR \fI<MAXIMUM_FREQUENCY_LINKAGE>\fR [default: 100]
`\-W`: maximum frequency difference in Hz allowed when linking two segments together
.TP
\fB\-\-onset\-release\-mode\fR \fI<ONSET_RELEASE_MODE>\fR [default: none]
`\-F`: how onset/release points are added to a segment
.TP
\fB\-\-onset\-duration\fR \fI<ONSET_DURATION>\fR [default: 0]
`\-u`: onset duration in seconds (only used when `\-\-onset\-release\-mode` isn\*(Aqt `none`)
.TP
\fB\-\-release\-duration\fR \fI<RELEASE_DURATION>\fR [default: 0]
`\-U`: release duration in seconds (only used when `\-\-onset\-release\-mode` isn\*(Aqt `none`)
.TP
\fB\-\-time\-shift\fR \fI<TIME_SHIFT>\fR [default: 0]
`\-n`: constant time shift in seconds applied to every written point\*(Aqs own timestamp
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIINPUT\fR>

